  "selection": {
    "rule": "Screen candidates on independent seeds and retain four useful area/performance choices. Require measured area at or below 295,000 GE, positive 10 MHz setup slack and passing pipeline and UART verification. The transition screen used 12 trial IDs, 14 backgrounds, 19 frequencies and five source levels.",
    "m30k18n512": "Low-area option. At -33 dBFS the long window localized 55.1% in the transition screen, compared with 35.3% for the roughly equal-area wide-aperture N256 option.",
    "m32k22w22f13": "Intermediate-area 32-mic option. Use lower accumulator precision to retain 22 bins. Transition-screen localization at -36 dBFS rose from 4.0% with 32 mics/18 bins to 9.5% with this configuration.",
    "m30k27w22f13": "Full spectral coverage in silicon. All 27 in-band bins fit using 22 total/13 fractional accumulator bits. It matched the 24/15 all-bin contender to the reported tenth of a percentage point at -36, -33 and -30 dBFS.",
    "m40k16n512": "Highest transition-screen localization among these four, with 22.6% at -36 dBFS and 72.9% at -33 dBFS. The 40/16 baseline with N256 scored 8.0% and 35.5% respectively."
  },
